-> Start

=== Start ===
[An elderly man stands near the graveyard, his gaze fixed on a single weathered gravestone. His shoulders are heavy, as if bearing the weight of years of grief. He doesn’t look up as you approach.]  
[[Elderly Man]]: You’ve come to this place, drawn like the others. The forest brought you, didn’t it?

* [What do you mean, “brought me”?] -> Option_Brought
* [No, I came of my own choice.] -> Option_Choice
* [Why are you here?] -> Option_WhyHere

=== Option_Brought ===
[[You]]: What do you mean, “brought me”?  
[[Elderly Man]]: No one comes here by chance. The forest has a way of calling to those with questions it might answer, or fears it might exploit.  
My name is Victor. I’ve seen many come and go, drawn by the same pull. Perhaps you’ll find what you seek, though I wouldn’t trust what it offers.  
-> AfterIntroduction

=== Option_Choice ===
[[You]]: No, I came of my own choice.  
[[Elderly Man]]: [Chuckles softly.] That’s what we all think, at first. But the forest… it whispers, even when we can’t hear it. You wouldn’t be here unless it wanted you to be.  
I’m Victor. Remember the name if the forest doesn’t take you first.  
-> AfterIntroduction

=== Option_WhyHere ===
[[You]]: Why are you here?  
[[Elderly Man]]: [Pauses, his voice heavy.] I stand here because she lies there. My wife. Two years gone. 
I’m Victor. I’ve stood here every day since, watching over her. The forest took her, like it takes everything in the end.  
-> AfterIntroduction

=== AfterIntroduction ===
[[Victor]]: You’ve seen the town, haven’t you? It’s a hollow shell. Families torn apart. Lives lost. That forest… it doesn’t just kill; it unravels us.  

* [How does the forest “take” people?] -> Option_Take
* [You seem to blame it for everything.] -> Option_Blame
* [I’m sorry for your loss.] -> Option_Sorry

=== Option_Take ===
[[You]]: How does the forest “take” people?  
[[Victor]]: It’s not just the wolves ors. It’s the way it seeps into you, plants its roots in your soul. It finds your weakness and pulls.  
For my wife, it was her dreams. She thought she could escape. She thought it whispered promises… but it lied.  
-> End

=== Option_Blame ===
[[You]]: You seem to blame it for everything.  
[[Victor]]: [Laughs bitterly.] Wouldn’t you? The forest is no mere place. It’s a predator. It takes what it wants, and it never gives it back.  
My family… my wife… the forest tore them apart, just like it’s torn this town to shreds.  
-> End

=== Option_Sorry ===
[[You]]: I’m sorry for your loss.  
[[Victor]]: [Nods slowly.] We all lose something here. Some lose their lives, others their hope. But thank you. It’s not often anyone stops to say that.  
-> End

=== End ===
Be careful, stranger. The forest has taken more than you can imagine, and it’s always hungry for more.  
[He turns back to the gravestone, his hand resting gently on its weathered surface.] 
I’ll stay here a while longer. You go on. Just… don’t let it take you too.  
-> END